+/*
+ * Samsara port: a built-in bitmap font, replacing fontconfig + freetype2.
+ *
+ * Upstream selects a font through fontconfig and rasterises it with freetype2.
+ * Neither library exists on Samsara, and porting either is a project in itself:
+ * fontconfig scans a font directory and parses configuration files, and
+ * freetype2 is a full TrueType rasteriser with its own build, its own memory
+ * management and its own file I/O. Doing that in order to draw ASCII would
+ * have been a far larger change than the terminal it was meant to serve, so
+ * this port replaces the whole mechanism with the one thing it needs: a bitmap
+ * font compiled in.
+ *
+ * The glyph data is the 8x8 printable-ASCII font already used by Samsara's own
+ * user-space console (user/nutcracker-rt/src/fb.rs, `FONT`). Reusing it is
+ * deliberate -- the kernel console, the installer wizard and fbterm then all
+ * render text the same way, so a screen does not change appearance depending on
+ * which program drew it.
+ *
+ * What this costs, stated plainly:
+ *
+ *   - No scalable fonts, and no font selection at all. The --font-names,
+ *     --font-size and --font-width/height/baseline options are accepted and
+ *     ignored, because accepting an option and warning about it is better than
+ *     refusing to start; see fbconfig.
+ *   - Printable ASCII only. A codepoint with no glyph returns NULL, which is
+ *     fbterm's own "draw the placeholder box" path, so unsupported text is
+ *     visibly wrong rather than silently blank.
+ *
+ * The cell is 8x16 with the 8-row glyph placed 4 rows down, so lines are
+ * spaced out and a descender has somewhere to go. An 8x8 cell would fit more
+ * rows on screen but reads as cramped.
+ */
+
